#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c44dd24-9762-5b0f-b8c3-c517b9b60ba1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=⟨1,-4,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327845} {:answer/id #uuid "36d4f699-5e4c-578c-81de-dd6dc5597532" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327846} {:answer/id #uuid "17782156-c5bc-52bc-b35a-443a7c32e894" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,2⟩=-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327847} {:answer/id #uuid "e4f58c9a-fc06-5d06-ba42-d722b09b44a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327848} {:answer/id #uuid "1ef10d49-a269-52f1-b2ec-680de72f81b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,2⟩=⟨-1,5,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36d4f699-5e4c-578c-81de-dd6dc5597532" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327846} :answer-field/id #uuid "d05dd2c3-a082-50ce-aad1-f27b3c1cd170" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b72bbef8-b4f4-5c9e-9fbc-de2a30c271f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-33317" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(1,-4,2)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(2,1,-3)$ and $B(1,6,-4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨1,-4,2⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(2,1,-3)$ and $B(1,6,-4)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,6,-4⟩-⟨2,1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,5,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-1,5,-1⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ & =⟨1,-4,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8774269b-3079-5838-8e20-b63286c329a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117607} {:answer/id #uuid "8c24e893-0b40-5d3f-a998-dcb0ba36e49d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117608} {:answer/id #uuid "1c742a2e-7c7b-58b7-bcc1-018a1b4c0473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117609} {:answer/id #uuid "7698e5e6-2811-503f-b463-d209ca3b1a58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117610} {:answer/id #uuid "7a04dcae-4de5-5376-bea3-a84f508e95ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a04dcae-4de5-5376-bea3-a84f508e95ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117611} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bd8acfb-e547-539e-b562-9ee71ef61e78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117606}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d32af589-36a2-5da2-a4fd-d2edd8386949" :question/math-academy-id "q-33319" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩=-14.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩=-14$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨6,-2,0⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ & =0 \\\\ 6{t}_{1}-2{t}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =3{t}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},3{t}_{1},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ eqauls $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,3,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{1}{3}.$"}]}
